course: dictionary
lesson: 11799
title: A word for a hat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A beret is a round, soft, flat hat with no brim, the edge that sticks out at the front of most hats. Berets are often made of wool or felt. «Grandpa wore a grey beret when he walked the dog.» The word beret tells you what kind of hat he wore.
explain: Context clues can help. «The soldiers all wore green berets as part of their uniform.» A uniform is the same clothes a group wears, so a beret can be part of a uniform. Check by swapping in a simpler word: «The soldiers all wore green hats as part of their uniform» still makes sense, so beret is a kind of hat.
explain: A picture can also give you a clue. In French lessons and pictures, a beret is a famous symbol of France, often shown with a striped top and a baguette. This is a cliché: it is a picture people often use, not what most French people wear today.
fact: A beret is a round, soft, flat hat without a brim.
fact: Berets are often made of wool or felt.
fact: Soldiers and Scouts wear berets as part of their uniform.
fact: «The Green Berets» is a name that links soldiers with this hat.
fact: In pictures, painters are often drawn wearing a beret, and a beret is a famous symbol of France, but most French people do not wear one today.
exercise: «Grandpa wore a grey beret when he walked the dog.» What is a beret? | A pair of warm gloves | A long, thin scarf | A pair of muddy boots | *A round, soft, flat hat with no brim
exercise: «The soldiers all wore green berets as part of their uniform.» What is a beret part of here? | A bedroom wall | A picnic, with food and drink | A school bag | *A uniform, the clothes a group wears together
exercise: What are berets often made of? | Paper and string | *Wool or felt | Glass | Sand
test: Why do many people link the beret with France? | Every person in France wears one to work | Berets can only be worn on Sundays | *Pictures of France often show someone in a beret with a striped top and a baguette | It is the name of a famous French river
test: In art, what do painters often get drawn wearing? | A crown | A tall chef's hat | A diving mask | *A beret
exam: Which meaning fits the word beret best? | A small wooden boat | A type of bread | A long, thin piece of cloth worn round the neck | *A round, soft, flat hat without a brim
